<section class="featured" id="systems">
  <div class="section-heading"><p>FEATURED PROJECTS</p><h2>Selected projects.</h2><span>Systems and automations I built to solve real needs in IT, manufacturing and day-to-day operations.</span></div>
  <div class="featured-list">
    <article class="feature-case feature-case--reverse"><div class="feature-case__copy"><div class="case-index"><span>01</span><span class="status status--internal">INTERNAL USE</span></div><p class="case-category">Inventory · Windows · IT support</p><h3>Belarc Inventory</h3><p class="case-summary">I co-developed a system that brings workstation inventory and technical context together to support IT service and maintenance.</p><div class="case-impact"><small>In practice</small><strong>Machine information is connected to support work, helping the team understand the device before taking action.</strong></div><p class="case-stack">Rust · Axum · SQLite · Windows</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="cases/belarc-inventory/">See how it works<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link text-link--muted" href="https://github.com/Mayconxzdev/Belarc-Inventory">View code<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="feature-case__visual"><figure class="case-showcase"><div class="case-showcase__frame"><img src="../assets/evidence/belarc-frota.jpg" alt="Sanitized workstation inventory dashboard with fictional data." loading="eager" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><span class="evidence-label">SANITIZED SCREEN · FICTIONAL DATA</span><strong>Inventory with context for IT support.</strong></figcaption></figure></div></article>

    <article class="feature-case feature-case--producao feature-case--reverse"><div class="feature-case__copy"><div class="case-index"><span>02</span><span class="status status--production">IN OPERATION</span></div><p class="case-category">Windows application · manufacturing · tracking</p><h3>Production Operations</h3><p class="case-summary">I deployed an application to organize production orders and share updates across the office, factory and a TV panel.</p><div class="case-impact"><small>In practice</small><strong>Office and production teams follow orders through a shared view.</strong></div><p class="case-stack">Python · PySide6 · SQLite · Windows</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="cases/producao-operacional/">See how it works<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link text-link--muted" href="https://github.com/Mayconxzdev/ProducaoOperacional">View code<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="feature-case__visual"><div class="visual visual--production"><div class="deployment-map"><div class="node"><small>OFFICE</small><b>Orders</b><span>entry and follow-up</span></div><div class="line"></div><div class="branches"><div class="node node--core"><small>SHARED WORKFLOW</small><b>Production</b><span>organized updates</span></div><div class="node"><small>FACTORY</small><b>Panel</b><span>shared view</span></div></div></div></div></div></article>

    <article class="feature-case feature-case--reverse"><div class="feature-case__copy"><div class="case-index"><span>03</span><span class="status status--production">IN USE AT WORK</span></div><p class="case-category">Industrial maintenance · equipment · records</p><h3>Field Maintenance</h3><p class="case-summary">I built an application to record maintenance carried out on machines and equipment, keeping the information organized for later reference.</p><div class="case-impact"><small>In practice</small><strong>Work records and history help the team follow what has been done on each piece of equipment.</strong></div><p class="case-stack">React · TypeScript · FastAPI · SQLite · PWA</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="cases/manutencao-campo/">See how it works<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link text-link--muted" href="https://github.com/Mayconxzdev/ManutencaoEmCampo">View public demo<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="feature-case__visual"><figure class="case-showcase"><div class="case-showcase__frame"><img src="../assets/evidence/campo-dashboard.webp" alt="Demonstration dashboard for the field maintenance application." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><span class="evidence-label">PUBLIC DEMO · FICTIONAL DATA</span><strong>Maintenance records and history.</strong></figcaption></figure></div></article>

    <article class="feature-case feature-case--postagem-redes"><div class="feature-case__copy"><div class="case-index"><span>04</span><span class="status status--pilot">FUNCTIONAL DEMO</span></div><p class="case-category">Applied AI · content automation</p><h3>Postagem Redes</h3><p class="case-summary">I built an automation that drafts content from approved context and keeps each channel’s workflow separate.</p><div class="case-impact"><small>In practice</small><strong>Content goes through human review before anything is published to social networks.</strong></div><p class="case-stack">n8n · APIs · RAG/grounding · OAuth2</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="cases/postagem-redes/">See how it works<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link text-link--muted" href="https://github.com/Mayconxzdev/PostagemRedes">View code<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="feature-case__visual"><div class="visual visual--social"><div class="publication-flow"><span>Context</span><i>→</i><span>Draft</span><i>→</i><span>Review</span><i>→</i><span>Publish</span></div><div class="visual-facts"><span>human approval</span><span>separate channel flows</span></div></div></div></article>
  </div>
</section>
